86455451 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455451 #edb/ref 1071 "Last year, a library had $8,000$ visitors. This year, the number of visitors is $25%$ greater than last year. How many visitors did the library have this year?\n\nThe library had\n{{field-1}}\nvisitors this year." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46812e7d-8475-5386-b10a-611a622fce90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455451 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the number of visitors this year, we apply a $25%$ increase to the previous year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $25%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+25%=125%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n125%=\\frac{125}{100}=1.25\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number of visitors by $1.25:$\n\n$$\n8,000\\times 1.25=10,000\n$$\n\nSo, the library had $10,000$ visitors this year." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $45%$ greater than $220?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5cc49cd7-e3e4-5fda-91a1-568bc252a9bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455458 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $45%$ *greater than* $220,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+45%=145%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n145%=\\frac{145}{100}=1.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $45%$ greater than $220,$ we multiply $220$ by $1.45:$\n\n$$\n1.45\\cdot 220=319\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $45%$ greater than $220$ is $319.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $12%$ greater than $1,500?$\n\nThe increased number is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "705623ab-2399-5c72-afa9-e085fef85022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455469 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $12%$ *greater than* $1,500,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+12%=112%.\n$$\n\nWe convert this percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n112%=\\frac{112}{100}=1.12\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number by $1.12:$\n\n$$\n1,500\\times 1.12=1,680\n$$\n\nSo, the number that is $12%$ greater than $1,500$ is $1,680.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1069 "q-318138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1071 "What number is $145%$ greater than $80?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b071ea5-55c1-5e38-adcd-b15bc3028d66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455476 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $145%$ *greater than* $80,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+145%=245%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n245%=\\frac{245}{100}=2.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $145%$ greater than $80,$ we multiply $80$ by $2.45:$\n\n$$\n2.45\\cdot 80=196\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $145%$ greater than $80$ is $196.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1071 "A lunch combo costs $$27$ before tax. If a $7%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price after tax?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93d6474a-bde5-548e-95ba-be3229625fd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455478 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $7%$ increase to the original cost.\n\nIncreasing by $7%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7%=107%=1.07\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.07:$\n\n$$\n27\\times 1.07=28.89.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price after tax is $$28.89.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1069 "q-327647" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1071 "A number $x$ is $400%$ greater than $120.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$  \n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9940990b-7568-5339-8565-7a872a78726e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455482 #edb/ref 1074 "To find a number $400%$ *greater than* $120,$ we apply a new percentage of  \n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting our percentage to a decimal:  \n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $400%$ greater than $120,$ we multiply $120$ by $5:$  \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 120=600\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=600.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1071 "A museum admission costs $$24$ before tax. If an $8.75%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price of the admission after tax?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb30e5e3-8d9a-5b05-b36b-6bb7841ecb74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455495 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $8.75%$ increase to the original price.\n\nIncreasing by $8.75%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+8.75%=108.75%=1.0875\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.0875:$\n\n$$\n24\\times 1.0875=26.1.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price of the admission after tax is $$26.10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-326514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1071 "A pair of shoes costs $$32$ before tax. If a $7.5%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total cost after tax?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d65902a0-bf9a-594a-840d-574205a14f9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455498 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the total cost after tax, we apply a $7.5%$ increase to the original price.\n\nIncreasing by $7.5%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7.5%=107.5%=1.075\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.075:$\n\n$$\n32\\times 1.075=34.4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total cost after tax is $$34.40.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1071 "An artist painted $60$ portraits last year. This year, her output is $400%$ greater than last year. How many portraits did the artist paint this year?\n\nThe artist painted\n{{field-1}}\nportraits this year." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f47719f0-1c2b-56f4-84a7-999378811070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455511 #edb/ref 1074 "To find this year's portrait output, we apply a $400%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $400%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $5:$\n\n$$\n60\\times 5=300\n$$\n\nSo, the artist painted $300$ portraits this year." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
